WEBVTT

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.440
<i>The year is 1889.</i>

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.570
<i>Nadia and Jean have arrived at a secret base at the South Pole.</i>

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:34.240
<i>There, Captain Nemo introduces them to the whale, Irion.</i>

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:39.950
<i>Irion predicts that Nada will meet her father and brother again.</i>

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:46.250
<i>The Nautilus continues its voyage in search of the Neo Atlanteans.</i>

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:57.550
You may start now.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:01.010
Sir, I shall begin with my economic distribution report.

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:04.850
Due to commercial disruption operations conducted by Garfish 1,

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:09.560
we've gained control of about 80% of the world trade in wool and other products.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:12.610
Export of armaments to various countries is proceeding smoothly.

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:16.360
Anticipated profits will reach three percent of our budget.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.240
At present, our Neo Atlantis operations

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.870
are moving one and one half percent of the total world currencies.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.700
Next, our military operations.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.210
About sixty percent of the final rigging

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:30.250
on our second aerial battleship is complete.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.960
It will be ready on schedule.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:41.720
Our fleet will be expanded by seven new Garfish within a few days.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:46.180
Construction has begun on the second burner for the Tower of Babel.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:48.690
What happened to the Nautilus?

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:55.110
Sir, we believe it was sunk. But no one has seen it.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:59.240
No one has seen the Nautilus sunk?

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:00.570
Knowing Nemo as well as I do,

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:05.830
he's probably hiding out some place trying to find out about us.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.930
Yes, Electra here.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.310
Good morning...

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:31.810
First Officer, sorry to bother you, but could you come to the bridge?

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:35.230
We've sighted what looks like a Garfish at 30,000 meters.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:37.280
I see. I'll be there right away.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:45.240
I just can't get up early in the morning. So sleepy...

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:51.250
Good morning.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.370
Morning.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:57.880
You think it's them?

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:58.920
I don't know.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:04.090
It's gone! A malfunction, maybe?

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.050
Could've been a whale.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.600
Check it out with the directional radio wave.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:10.100
Aye.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:15.730
Let's all play 'Who Laughs First!'

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.870
That Jean.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:37.380
He's always reading books, or working on some new invention.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.130
He never comes around to play with us.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.260
Is something wrong?

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.970
Hey, Nadia...

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:50.930
Nadia, why don't you join us too?

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:58.270
I know. You're feeling low because Jean doesn't come by, right?

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:01.480
It's not that at all!

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:12.200
Marie, I'm sorry. I'm really sorry!

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.710
Please don't cry. Okay? Okay?

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:21.380
I know what, Marie. Let's go and see Jean.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:22.510
Okay, Marie?

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:28.300
I swear! Whoever taught you to cry like that?

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:31.060
Mr. Sanson taught me.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:36.980
He told me that you have to do some lying and cheating to get along.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:42.070
Those people teach you the most awful things.

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:47.360
I wonder if I'm catching cold?

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:53.490
But just think, I can wash for my beloved Captain Nemo.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.580
I must be the luckiest person on Earth!

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.590
We must be the unluckiest, being forced to help her like this.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:06.010
Why must I, the playboy Sanson, be washing clothes?

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.800
Don't be so conceited!

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.850
Modern girls like men who help with housework!

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:19.770
Of course, with sailors like Captain Nemo, it's quite different.

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.610
How's it going, Jean?

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:27.860
Just perfect!

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:32.330
This will be finished very soon. Everything is going as I planned.

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:37.540
By 'this', you mean something that flies?

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.000
That's right.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:42.080
But this one doesn't even have a propeller.

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:46.380
In this new invention, air and fuel are burned inside this unit,

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:50.050
and the flame is forced out the back. The reaction makes it fly.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:53.010
This special automatic valve is the key.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:56.770
The output is still too weak to carry a human being.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:03.610
It's not going to be another one of your failures, is it?

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:05.820
Don't worry, the theory is perfect.

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:11.490
Nadia, with this invention, I'll surely take you to Africa.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.200
There, it's finished!

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.200
Ready for take-off.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.580
So, it's ready now?

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:20.790
Yes, we can start testing now.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:33.470
It works!

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:36.430
Wonderful! It's actually flying!

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:39.140
Of course it is!

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:41.690
My theory is perfect!

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:42.770
Amazing!

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.070
What?

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:51.530
I knew this would happen.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:55.660
Look out!

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:12.510
What have you done?

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:21.980
What was that?

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:22.940
An enemy attack?

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:33.990
I'm sorry.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:35.950
What was that noise?

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:39.540
It seems that one of Jean's inventions had a slight accident.

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:42.040
It sure gave us a big scare.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:48.460
Unknown contact restored.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:51.050
Can you tell if it's really a Garfish?

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:54.010
Perhaps they pinpointed us through that explosion.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:55.010
That's possible.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:01.310
Well, don't be so upset.

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:02.310
That's right!

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:06.690
You know what they say about learning from your mistakes, Jean?

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.650
Don't worry, it's okay.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:13.400
I expected something like this, and secretly prepared a spare engine.

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:18.820
Jean, the reason your first test plane failed

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:21.790
is because you were relying too much on your reserve unit.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.500
You really think so?

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.960
What a deceitful person!

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.000
I agree.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:35.380
Emergency dive! Emergency dive! All personnel on deck, take cover!

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:36.220
Oh, no!

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:39.430
Whee! It's like a race! Hurry! Hurry! Hurry!

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:40.180
Let's get inside!

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:41.060
What happened?

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:42.390
Senorita, hurry!

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:45.850
Of all things! I just rewashed them!

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.520
Leave those things!

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.440
You can always find clothes to wash.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:53.650
Oh, Nemo's precious clothes!
Nemo's precious clothes!

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:56.360
I'm going back! Let me go!

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:15.170
Depth 50 meters. One-third cruising speed.

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.930
12,000 to Garfish's position.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:19.640
It's coming toward us on a collision course.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:21.930
Have they located us?

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:24.520
I can't tell. Any sonar response?

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:25.430
None.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:27.020
Shall we shoot first?

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:31.480
They don't know that we've returned to full battle condition.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:36.570
That's right. We can utilize that and attack with full force.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:41.200
We don't know where Gargoyle is. We can't act on wishful thinking.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:47.410
Their force outnumbers us twenty to one. What other way is there?

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:49.250
There isn't any!

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.550
That's a directional sonar.

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:58.010
I think they've located us.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.220
How could they?

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:04.180
We must act. Take battle positions!

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:07.390
What? You've located the Nautilus?

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:10.020
Yes, Sir. A report has come in from Garfish 28.

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:15.360
"Have located Nautilus. Will engage it in battle."

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:20.360
So Nemo still lives.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:24.200
Continue with your report.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.080
Yes, Sir.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:32.040
According to our study made on Tower of Babel I, which exploded...

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:39.420
Excuse me, Sir, but communication from Garfish 28 has ceased.

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:42.130
It has probably been sunk.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:45.180
Damn Nemo and his Nautilus.

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:48.890
They are certainly a thorn in our side.

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:51.980
On the other hand, if the Nautilus is still active,

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:55.860
we can use it to test the power of our flying battleship.

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:58.070
Maybe you're right.

00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:00.900
This is the time to put an end to the games.

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:03.490
We're not playing games!

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:05.990
Do you understand that?

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:07.910
What was that?

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:09.250
Yes, Sir!

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:10.660
Really...

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:12.580
That's enough.

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:13.420
Yes, Sir!

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:15.170
Jean...

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:16.420
Yes, Sir!

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:19.880
You realize what you have done, don't you?

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:21.090
Yes, Sir.

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:26.550
Even a small mistake can sometimes affect the lives of many people.

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:28.310
Don't ever forget that.

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:29.140
Yes, Sir.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.850
Then, you are excused.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:33.100
Yes, Sir.

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:38.270
Jean received a scolding from Nemo? Then what happened?

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:40.730
Yeah, now he's making another airplane.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:44.860
In spite of that, he's making another airplane.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:47.070
The kid has a lot of spunk.

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:48.870
You're the child!

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:50.580
Right, Papa?

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:55.250
Now, we're going to have our dinner.

00:12:56.710 --> 00:13:02.260
Why must I, a famous dandy, be playing at games like this?

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:05.880
My reputation will be ruined.

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:08.100
Right?

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:11.890
Hey, Hanson, you take my place for a while!

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:15.940
Okay, as soon as I make a liquid version of hard tectite.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:20.480
Trying to outdo Jean in inventions!

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:24.150
I wonder if Electra would like to take my place?

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:26.610
I don't like that lady. She looks scary.

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:30.530
She's always after us to study.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:33.160
Listen to her.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:35.910
She's a well brought up young lady.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:40.040
So, where's Nadia?

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:42.130
She's with Jean.

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:46.720
These young couples in love!
How happy they must be!

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:48.390
Why couldn't you be more aggressive?

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:50.680
You just stood there saying, "Yes, yes, yes!" to everything he said!

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:54.930
You didn't do it on purpose!
Why didn't you stand up to him?

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:56.810
You're just afraid of him!

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:00.770
What can I say? It was my fault.

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:02.980
You give up too easily!

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:05.940
No, it's just that I'm still a kid.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:09.370
My hair is bothering me.

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:14.200
All right, I'll go and see Captain Nemo!

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:15.660
Nadia!

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:23.130
What's wrong, Nadia?

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:25.840
Where's Captain Nemo?

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:28.300
Probably in the captain's cabin.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.010
Captain's cabin?

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:42.150
Captain Nemo, Nadia is here. She wants to talk to you.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:44.190
All right, I'm coming.

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:56.330
Tell me why Jean is in the wrong!

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:58.160
Can't you see that for yourself?

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:02.380
No, I cannot see that! Why must he receive such a scolding?

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:05.590
If you can't see that, it's no use explaining to you now.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:07.800
You're just trying to evade my question!

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:10.260
You're wrong, Nadia. Calm down.

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:13.470
He gave away your position to a Garfish.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:15.470
So what? You destroyed it anyway!

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:19.560
Nadia, children shouldn't say such things.

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:21.600
Grown-ups are always like that.

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:27.030
When we ask something inconvenient, they say we're too young.

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:28.490
It's not fair!

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:30.530
I really hate grown-ups!

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:43.170
Nadia, please don't say such sad things.

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:49.050
And then you came running back here?

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:54.260
There was a time in my life when I felt that way,

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:57.720
when everything that grown-ups did seemed unfair and underhanded.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.930
You mean you passed through such a time too?

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:04.650
Don't be rude. I'm still in my 20's.

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:06.110
I'm sorry.

00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:09.900
That's okay. I found it hard to forgive them too.

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:13.950
Eventually, I realized that there was a reason for acting like that.

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:18.240
There's a reason for the way grown-ups act.

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:23.290
There will come a time when you too will feel, "I was young then."

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:29.550
What's your boyfriend, Jean, doing at an important time like this?

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:33.880
I think he's still with Miss Electra.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:38.470
I see. Be careful she doesn't steal Jean away from you.

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:44.520
Jean lost his mother when he was young. He has a mother complex.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:46.310
What's that?

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:51.360
You don't know? It means men who long for older girls.

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:53.950
That vixen!

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:59.120
She not only makes eyes at Captain Nemo, but goes after boys too!

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:01.700
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:03.410
What's the matter?

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:07.830
It's strange. I felt as if someone were talking about me.

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:11.260
It must be someone saying how beautiful you are.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:15.720
Don't flatter me. You should be saying things like that to Nadia.

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:22.350
It's no use saying such things to Nadia! She'll think I'm lying.

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:26.940
Jean, there is no girl who doesn't want to hear such things.

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:29.690
Try!

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:32.110
All right?

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:37.530
What are you doing?

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:42.330
I was just asking her about the ether.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:44.620
You're lying. Look at your hair.

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:48.290
She was cutting your hair!

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:51.550
You're always finding excuses for visiting her room.

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:52.800
You're despicable!

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:55.470
That's not true!

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:57.880
I wonder! Right, King?

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:04.390
Nadia, you're looking very nice today.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:08.100
Just beautiful!

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:12.190
What's wrong, Jean? You have a fever or something?

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:17.280
No, I was told that all girls like to hear nice things about them.

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:18.740
Who told you that?

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:20.070
Miss Electra.

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:25.540
Jean...

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.210
I hate you!

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:37.470
Why?

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:41.350
Miss Electra, you lied to me.

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:48.520
Why, Jean? Why? Why?

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:50.980
Why are you always with Miss Electra?

00:18:57.490 --> 00:18:58.950
Come in.

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:00.780
Oh!

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:03.490
Welcome. This is a pleasant surprise.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:08.410
Did Jean say anything to you?

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:11.380
That's what I came to see you about.

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:14.340
I see. Shall we go take a bath?

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:16.250
A bath?

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:19.220
Fun!

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:25.970
Miss Electra?

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:30.060
How do you feel about Jean?

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:33.230
Like a younger brother, I think.

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:35.190
A younger brother?

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:40.490
Then, don't put funny ideas into his head.

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:44.830
What are your feelings toward Jean?

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:48.410
J- Just a friend.

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:51.120
I see.

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:55.250
What are your feelings about Captain Nemo?

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:59.720
I like him very much.

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:02.720
Does that seem odd?

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.050
But he's such a cold person!

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:07.100
A cold person?

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:09.640
I guess you're right.

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:12.520
But he has suffered so much.

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:17.980
He has caused the death of many people,

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:21.360
but he is prepared to take full responsibility for his actions.

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:26.280
If it wasn't for him, I wouldn't be alive today.

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:30.910
He has saved me many times over the past thirteen years.

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:34.170
After facing so much,

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:37.710
why must you pursue Gargoyle and the Neo Atlantis forces in battle?

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:41.840
Someone has to stop him and his inhuman plans.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:45.800
The only one able to cope with him and his science is this Nautilus.

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:47.890
That's the banner of our cause.

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:49.600
Banner of your cause?

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:51.600
Banner of your cause?

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:56.060
When we undertake a mission, we must have a banner for our cause.

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:00.480
But that's not the only reason.

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:02.900
It's revenge.

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:04.110
Revenge?

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:08.120
That's right. Once I had a younger brother.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:11.910
Had? Where is he now?

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:16.040
Thirteen years ago, he went to the same place as my parents.

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:17.080
Where's that?

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:19.290
The bottom of a lake.

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:25.800
Thirteen years ago, one man came and destroyed our hometown.

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:27.430
That's when they died.

00:21:28.090 --> 00:21:29.720
And that person was Gargoyle?

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:31.180
What a monster!

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:36.650
Yes, truly a monster!

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:39.230
And Captain Nemo rescued you?

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:42.730
Yes, but I was not the only one left alive.

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:47.860
The remaining ones gathered together and built this ship

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:52.830
as a weapon to take revenge on Gargoyle and his Neo Atlanteans.

00:21:55.250 --> 00:21:57.250
Let me wash your face.

00:21:57.670 --> 00:21:59.500
Be still, will you?

00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:04.670
Captain Nemo,

00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:10.300
how much longer are you going to keep those children on board?

00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:16.020
It's true that Nadia is a target and it's safer on board,

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:20.360
but we don't know when this ship will be sunk.

00:22:21.650 --> 00:22:25.240
I'm sure you don't intend to let her die with you?

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:30.740
Approaching ship identified as Garfish-class.

00:22:30.740 --> 00:22:33.620
Captain, please come to the bridge immediately.

00:22:34.290 --> 00:22:35.910
I'll be right there.

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:37.370
Captain Nemo!

00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:40.330
Order everyone to battle positions, First Officer.

00:22:40.330 --> 00:22:41.960
Yes, Sir.

00:22:45.710 --> 00:22:48.430
Incredible! I count a total of six enemy vessels.

00:22:48.430 --> 00:22:51.220
There are enemy ships in every direction.

00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:53.890
Maximum depth in these waters is three hundred meters.

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:57.850
Captain, we have the Kermodec Trench at 10 o'clock.

00:22:58.810 --> 00:23:01.810
Head for the Kermodec Trench at full speed.

00:23:01.810 --> 00:23:02.520
Aye, Sir.

00:23:07.360 --> 00:23:11.200
The Nautilus is headed for the Kermodec Trench just as we planned.

00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:14.870
The mouse is speeding into our trap.

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:20.420
In a little while, it will be the end for you, Nemo.

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:22.830
Order everyone to battle positions!

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:24.040
Yes, Sir.

00:23:24.840 --> 00:23:26.960
All personnel, take battle positions.

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:29.420
All personnel prepare for submarine warfare.

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:33.470
All non-combatants, proceed to Block 3 shelter.

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:36.810
This battle is going to be dangerous.

00:23:37.270 --> 00:23:38.270
Why?

00:23:38.680 --> 00:23:40.810
I feel a different tension in the air.

00:23:40.810 --> 00:23:45.520
Yes, and the number of sonar pings hitting us this time is greater.

00:24:04.290 --> 00:24:08.210
Gargoyle is attacking with his full force trying to sink us.
